init-chkroot: open the multiboot menu (bootmenu) before reading STARTUP

The original chkroot init (initramfs-mipsel.cpio.xz of meta-vuplus) is kept;
only the bootmenu call is added: the startup vfat partition is mounted on
/boot, vu_ir is loaded (bootmenu loads vu_fb), bootmenu may copy a
STARTUP_x to STARTUP, then everything is unloaded and the chkroot logic
goes on unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [kexec-multiboot]

--- a/init-chkroot.sh
+++ b/init-chkroot.sh
@@ -76,6 +76,22 @@
 echo "[init] BOOT found:$BOOT" > /dev/console
 echo "[init] ROOTFSTYPE found:$ROOTFSTYPE" > /dev/console
 
+# kexec-multiboot: multiboot menu (vu_fb/vu_ir + bootmenu) on the startup partition.
+# bootmenu copies the chosen STARTUP_x to STARTUP; the chkroot logic below reads it.
+if [ -n "$BOOT" ] && [ -x /usr/bin/bootmenu ]; then
+  mkdir -p /boot
+  if mount -t vfat "$BOOT" /boot 2>/dev/null; then
+    KDIR=/lib/modules/`uname -r`/extra
+    insmod $KDIR/vu_ir.ko
+    /usr/bin/bootmenu --root /boot
+    echo "[init] bootmenu exit code $? (10 = STARTUP changed)" > /dev/console
+    rmmod vu_ir 2>/dev/null
+    rmmod vu_fb 2>/dev/null
+    sync
+    umount /boot
+  fi
+fi
+
 mkdir -p /boot
 if mount -t vfat "$BOOT" /boot 2>/dev/null; then
   echo "[init] $BOOT mounted as FAT" > /dev/console
